## Why This Is Asked

Stack growth is a core OS mechanism; understanding it reveals how memory safety and performance interact in practice.

## Key Concepts

- Stack growth policy and guard pages
- RLIMIT_STACK and address space layout
- Page fault handling and page-table updates
- TLB invalidation and re-execution
- Concurrency with multiple threads touching stack boundaries

## Code Example

```javascript
// high-level pseudo
if (fault_addr in stack && allowed) {
  pa = alloc_page();
  map(p, pa, fault_addr_page, 'RW');
  zero_page(pa);
  flush_tlb(p, fault_addr_page);
} else {
  handle_fault_error();
}
```

